  "body": "Found in the review of PR #576 (#571).\n\n**Today:** locate (#561, PR #566) warns by name when the part or its stock would sink into a fixture. A plain Model-page `MoveModel` (move or turn) runs no such check. Since #571 (PR #576) a turned part's square stock is refitted around it, so the regrown block could enter a vise jaw or floor with no warning. The old rigid tilt had the same gap, so this is not a regression.\n\n**Expected:** `MoveModel` runs the same sampled part-and-stock-versus-fixture check as locate and warns by name: the moved body, the fixture and a point. A warning, not a refusal, as with locate.\n\n**Done means:** a test moves or turns a part so its stock enters a fixture and gets the by-name warning; a clear move gets none.",
